-Implemented the safe RGBA frame API and CoreGraphics presentation path inside `vexel-platform-apple`. The work-order validator passed. The focused package check and tests were blocked because the requested offline `CARGO_HOME` could not resolve `bitflags`, so the new unit tests did not run.
+# Result
+
+Fixed the Apple frame presentation candidate. `RgbaFrame` now documents and
+accepts Vexel's top-left, tightly packed straight-alpha sRGB RGBA8 pixels.
+Before image construction the presenter deterministically premultiplies RGB;
+CoreGraphics receives those bytes with `PremultipliedLast` metadata in sRGB.
+Frame validation checks exact byte length and allocated `Vec` capacity against
+the existing 64 MiB bound. The layer image is fully prepared before native
+properties change; guarded failure handling restores contents, scale, and
+gravity while retaining the previous image. Unsafe extern-static reads and
+other unsafe boundaries have concrete safety comments. Changed source files
+remain below 800 lines.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `CARGO_HOME="$PWD/../../../.cache/cargo" CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$PWD/.cache/build" cargo +stable check -p vexel-platform-apple --locked --offline` — exit 0, clean with no warnings.
+- `CARGO_HOME="$PWD/../../../.cache/cargo" CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$PWD/.cache/build" cargo +stable test -p vexel-platform-apple --locked --offline` — exit 0, 35 unit tests, 5 native-boundary tests, 1 native-window test, and 6 doc tests passed (47 total).
+- `python3 scripts/wo_validate.py WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01 --ready` — exit 0; revision 1 and frozen work-order hash validated.
 
-The exact logs, result summary, ownership notes, and affected-file hashes are in [artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01](/Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.cache/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01/worker/artifacts/WO-RUST-APPLE-PRESENTATION-01). No live AppKit rendering was verified.
\ No newline at end of file
+The semi-transparent deterministic case verifies straight `[200, 100, 50, 128]`
+input remains unchanged at the public frame boundary and encodes to
+`[100, 50, 25, 128]` for CoreGraphics. Capacity validation rejects a vector
+whose allocation exceeds 64 MiB even when its pixel length is otherwise valid.
+
+Input ownership is transferred into `RgbaFrame`; `present_rgba` consumes it.
+The conversion stays in the owned vector, `CFData::new` copies bytes
+synchronously, `CGDataProvider` retains the CFData, and the layer retains its
+published CGImage. Rows preserve visual top-to-bottom order; color data is
+sRGB and CoreGraphics receives premultiplied-last alpha. There is no live
+AppKit runtime proof; package checks do not establish interactive rendering.
+
