-Implemented the safe RGBA frame API and CoreGraphics presentation path inside `vexel-platform-apple`. The work-order validator passed. The focused package check and tests were blocked because the requested offline `CARGO_HOME` could not resolve `bitflags`, so the new unit tests did not run.
+# Result
+
+Fixed the Apple frame presentation candidate. `RgbaFrame` now documents and
+accepts Vexel's top-left, tightly packed straight-alpha sRGB RGBA8 pixels.
+Before image construction the presenter deterministically premultiplies RGB;
+CoreGraphics receives those bytes with `PremultipliedLast` metadata in sRGB.
+Frame validation checks exact byte length and allocated `Vec` capacity against
+the existing 64 MiB bound. The layer image is fully prepared before native
+properties change; guarded failure handling restores contents, scale, and
+gravity while retaining the previous image. Unsafe extern-static reads and
+other unsafe boundaries have concrete safety comments. Changed source files
+remain below 800 lines.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `CARGO_HOME="$PWD/../../../.cache/cargo" CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$PWD/.cache/build" cargo +stable check -p vexel-platform-apple --locked --offline` — exit 0, clean with no warnings.
